"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.012032840261649459,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":62.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.040365426860539864,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":56.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.010083303334859184,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":62.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00246,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":1.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Diageo plc, together with its subsidiaries, engages in the production, marketing, and distribution of alcoholic beverages in North America, Europe, the Asia Pacific, Latin America and Caribbean, and Africa. It offers beer, scotch, gin, vodka, rum, liqueur, raki, wine, cacha\u00e7a, tequila, brandy, and Chinese white spirit beverages, as well as Irish, Canadian, Chinese US, and Indian whisky. The company also provides ready-to-drink and non-alcoholic beverages. Its principal brands include Johnnie Walker, Don Julio, Guinness, Crown Royal, Smirnoff, Baileys, Captain Morgan, Buchanan's, Casamigos, Shui Jing Fang, and McDowell's. The company was formerly known as Guinness plc and changed its name to Diageo plc in February 1998. The company was incorporated in 1886 and is headquartered in London, the United Kingdom.","ceo_bio":"Sir David John Lewis | CEO & Executive Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $2.9M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 27K people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Defensive peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Diageo plc is a large-cap consumer defensive business with a $55.5B market cap on $28.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 7% cost of capital, a 9-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 41%.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.0\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.0% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.4\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Carries a 1465% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":14.650240031351032},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Input cost inflation from agricultural commodities \u2014 when raw materials spike, pass-through pricing lags and margin compression is immediate.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 13% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 31% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","28 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Consumer Defensive tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Diageo (LSE:DGE) Grapples With Rising UK Competition And Weather Hit To Sales","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/gb/food-beverage-tobacco/lse-dge/diageo-shares/news/diageo-lsedge-grapples-with-rising-uk-competition-and-weathe","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793985920.146,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.735,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Earnings Beat Altering The Investment Case For Diageo (LSE:DGE)?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/earnings-beat-altering-investment-case-131145075.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793970705.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.866,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Diageo (LSE:DGE) Stock May Be 36% Undervalued As Rival Stout Pressure Builds","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/diageo-lse-dge-stock-may-121555769.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793967355.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.153,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Diageo 2026 AGM: Unanimous Approval of All 25 Shareholder Resolutions","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kal